# Competency question: "What are the linking properties of the study spine — how are
# population, frame, sample, unit, variable, and missingness wired together?" Exercises the
# object properties that keep the target of inference distinct from the thing measured: a
# math:StatisticalPopulation is operationalized by a frame (math:samplingFrame), a
# math:Sample is drawn from that frame (math:sampleOf), refers to the population
# (math:population), and denotes an observation unit (math:observationUnit) recording a
# variable (math:statisticalVariable), whose absences are carried by a missingness indicator
# (math:hasMissingnessIndicator) resting on a mechanism (math:missingnessMechanism). The query
# projects each PREDICATE, scoped to the spine subjects and the math: namespace. Over the
# fixture the answer is exactly the seven spine-linking property edges.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX ex:   <http://example.org/math/>

SELECT ?subject ?prop ?object WHERE {
    VALUES ?subject { ex:pop ex:sample ex:var }
    ?subject ?prop ?object .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?prop), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?subject ?prop ?object
